pic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2140"} "National Speed Skating Oval, Olympic Green, Beijing"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19020425"} "30 from 17 countries"]]] [:tr {:class "records", :style ""} [:th {:style "vertical-align: top;"} "Olympic Record "] [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9001054"} "1:13.56"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/119771"} "Jorien ter Mors"] " " [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"] " / 14 February 2018 / " [:a {:href "/records/event_name/538"} "Details"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/1805305"} "Trevis Boyd"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Starter"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/1805306"} "Bartosz Dawidowski"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POL.png"}] "POL"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Prior to the race, two skaters were named most likely to win the 1,000 m. Dutchwoman " [:a {:href "/athletes/148673"} "Jutta Leerdam"] " had won the world title in 2020 (and was second in 2021), and with a fifth place in the 500 m had shown good form. Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/119701"} "Miho Takagi"] " had already secured three silver medals (500 m, 1,500 m and team pursuit) and was looking to win her first individual Olympic gold medal. An outsider was " [:a {:href "/athletes/128778"} "Brittany Bowe"] ". Although a three-time world champion in the event (2015, 2019, 2021), and leader in the 2021/22 1,000 m World Cup, Bowe’s performances in the Beijing Olympics had been below expectations."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The first top time of the day was recorded by 1,500 m bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/128166"} "Antoinette de Jong"] " in pair three, with 1:14.92. This remained unchallenged until Leerdam took the ice against " [:a {:href "/athletes/149162"} "Kimi Goetz"] " in the 11th pair. After a tight crossing with Goetz, Leerdam made a small mishap in the third corner, touching the ice briefly with her hand. Despite this, she recorded the fastest full lap of the field, holding on for a final time of 1:13.83."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Two pairs later, it was Takagi’s turn. After recording the fastest opening of the day (17.60) together with " [:a {:href "/athletes/128402"} "Golikova"] ", she paced her full lap a bit, trailing Leerdam by 0.01 at the bell. But with an excellent final lap, she clearly went into the lead, 1:13.19. Bowe, racing in the last pair, had the same opening as Golikova and Takagi, but lost nearly half a second in the first lap. But Golikova’s final lap had been almost three seconds slower than her first, which was exploited by Bowe, who clocked 1:14.61, a tenth faster than the ROC athlete, to win her first individual Olympic medal, a bronze."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button732931", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button732931').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "200 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "600 m"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "13"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/119701"} "Miho Takagi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "1:13.19"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} 